UID:57144-1776711600-1776718800@visitlancastercity.com
SUMMARY:Revolutionary Lancaster Lecture
DESCRIPTION:Historic Rock Ford’s America250 Lecture Series welcomes Benton G. Webber as he presents “Revolutionary Lancaster.” Lancaster County was not the site of any military battles of our country’s Revolutionary War\, but the community was impacted in almost every other way possible. Come and learn about life here 250 years ago and how it was turned upside down as “the course of human events” at the global and national scale came crashing down right here in Lancaster\, disrupting the lives of many in order to secure “certain unalienable rights.” \n\n\n\nThis presentation will begin at 7 PM in the Langmuir Education Room located on the first floor of the Rock Ford Barn. Admission is for the lecture only and does not include the Snyder Gallery.  
URL:https://visitlancastercity.com/event/revolutionary-lancaster-lecture/
LOCATION:Historic Rock Ford\, 881 Rockford Road\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:History
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitlancastercity.com/wp-content/uploads/America250-Revolutionary-Lancaster.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Historic Rock Ford":MAILTO:office@HistoricRockFord.org
END:VEVENT
